        "how_justification": "Parses wine_findings.csv with csv.read_rows and applies table_equals: every graded cell of 39 rows plus the full 43-row population as a row_set lock (a duplicated or missing wine fails the lock), and the delivered column set closed to the stated header, with the finding cell compared as text (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed). A failure names the exact row.",
        "why_justification": "Every wine's finding under WM1-WM3 on its governing line, with codes joined in policy order, is graded. Entailed by: \"One row per wine, keyed by `wine_id` as `wine_purchases.csv` writes it, in any order. A wine that appears on more than one line of the purchasing table is one wine and one row ... joined with `|` in policy order\"",
        "tag": "core"
      },
